1
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,999
Claire said she wanted to go back to work.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,159
<i>Are you crazy?</i>

3
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:15,959
You want me to go back to work?

4
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:19,079
<i>Someone leaked that Claire hired
Yo and Patchy to be her friends.</i>

5
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:20,999
Socialite Claire's back in the news?

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,159
Ms. Claire's really here!

7
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:24,159
Ms. Claire, can we get a statement?

8
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:27,199
<i>I'm here to demand justice for my friend.</i>

9
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:31,359
My friend is dead,
and yet nobody is saying a word about it.

10
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:33,159
<i>I'm worried about one thing.</i>

11
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:34,320
She won't tell her the truth, right?

12
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:48,040
Are you doing okay?

13
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,720
I mean,

14
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:58,480
my people didn't hurt you, right?

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:00,839
Ms. Claire,

16
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:03,439
if you have something to say to me,
just say it.

17
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:05,880
Don't beat around the bush.

18
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,400
If you don't mind,

19
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:13,639
could you tell me

20
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:16,560
what happened
after the helicopter crash that day?

21
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:22,160
And why do you want to know?

22
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:26,960
Well, you want me to take responsibility.

23
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:29,479
I was unconscious for months.

24
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:31,359
If I had known sooner,

25
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:36,080
I would've tried to get in touch
and take responsibility, like you wanted.

26
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:43,039
Do you really want to know,

27
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:46,640
or... are you just playing a part?

28
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:50,800
I really want to know.

29
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:53,879
Before the crash,

30
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:58,400
Ms. Jinla told me
if she died, nobody would care.

31
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,000
What?

32
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,600
Jin told you that?

33
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,760
Jin told you that?

34
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:28,120
How could she not know
how devastated I would be?

35
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:33,159
<i>Jin, how did the interview
with Ms. Khaedarun go?</i>

36
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:35,999
<i>Are you done? Tell me all about it.</i>

37
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:36,919
It's been hours.

38
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:39,120
Why haven't you replied, Jin?

39
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:42,839
<i>We have some breaking news.</i>

40
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:46,239
<i>A helicopter carrying
Ms. Khaedarun Kanchathara,</i>

41
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,839
<i>an executive of TGL Group,</i>

42
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:52,239
<i>has crashed in the Nakhon Nayok area.</i>

43
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:55,599
<i>We understand there are
two confirmed fatalities:</i>

44
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:58,519
<i>the pilot and a member
of Ms. Khaedarun's team</i>

45
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:01,679
<i>who flew out with her for an interview.</i>

46
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:05,560
<i>We will bring you more updates
as soon as they become available.</i>

47
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,880
<i>Despite the news report,</i>

48
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:12,479
<i>I refused to believe my friend was gone.</i>

49
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:14,879
<i>She died, and you're not
gonna take responsibility?</i>

50
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:18,519
<i>Because I wanted to believe
a miracle would happen for her.</i>

51
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,240
<i>But in the end,</i>

52
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:26,600
- <i>miracles aren't real.</i>
- Jin.

53
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:29,919
I'm so sorry.

54
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:32,040
<i>But you know what was real?</i>

55
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,720
<i>Your inhumanity.</i>

56
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:38,960
None of you has even bothered
to offer her an apology.

57
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:45,640
My friend Jinla was a good person.

58
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,920
And I never thought...

59
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:53,640
we'd be torn apart so soon.

60
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:14,440
I...

61
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:19,520
I sympathize and...

62
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:22,240
I'm sorry you lost your best friend.

63
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:28,160
But you know it was an accident, right?

64
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:32,679
And since it was an accident,
you have no right to demand anything.

65
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:33,920
So what?

66
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:40,160
Are you calling the cops to arrest me?

67
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:42,840
Go ahead. Call them right now.

68
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:47,320
No.

69
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:54,800
I know you're doing this
because you feel guilty about Ms. Jinla.

70
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:03,560
Why would I feel guilty about her?

71
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:08,000
Because it was you...

72
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:11,880
who should've been on that chopper.

73
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:15,160
You were supposed to interview me,

74
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,960
but you made Ms. Jinla go instead.

75
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:22,599
If you want to repay me,

76
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:24,440
I have a job for you.

77
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,160
What job?

78
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,560
Socialite Claire.

79
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:31,240
Khaedarun Kanchathara.

80
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:52,560
How did you know about that?

81
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:57,480
Ms. Jinla told me that day.

82
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:16,960
Do you have any more questions?

83
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:21,880
If not,

84
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:24,240
I'll take my leave.

85
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:26,480
Ms. Wan.

86
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,280
Thank you.

87
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:38,200
For what?

88
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:42,040
Nothing.

89
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:46,640
I just feel like if I were Ms. Jinla,

90
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:51,000
I would want to thank you
for loving her so much.

91
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:58,680
And please...

92
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:02,480
don't feel guilty.

93
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,320
It was an accident.

94
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:09,040
Stop blaming yourself.

95
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,159
Are you okay?

96
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:51,279
What were you two talking about?

97
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,640
Why did she...?

98
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:56,480
She's not mad at Ms. Claire.

99
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:04,000
She's mad at herself.

100
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:06,480
Actually,

101
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:09,680
the one who was supposed
to be on that chopper was...

102
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,240
Wan.

103
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:15,200
But she made me go instead.

104
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:20,120
So she thinks I died because of her.

105
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,839
Ms. Wan really cares about you.

106
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:33,640
I didn't get a chance to tell you
that I met Ms. Wan at your house,

107
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:37,360
She was being harassed by your creditors.

108
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:44,080
Did... did they do anything to her?

109
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,440
Not yet.

110
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,959
They wanted her to pay off your debt.

111
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:52,000
No, they can't do that.

112
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:55,519
I need to talk to them.

113
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:56,879
There's no need.

114
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:59,040
I already taught them a lesson.

115
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:03,439
But what I'm trying to tell you is,

116
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:06,640
even though she thinks you're dead,

117
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:11,680
she's still doing her best
to protect that house for you.

118
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:32,040
Hey,

119
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,880
I'm begging you.

120
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:37,640
Please let it go this time.

121
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:40,800
I don't want her to get a criminal record.

122
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:45,960
- Please...
- Don't say another word.

123
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:52,640
Tun.

124
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:58,160
Do what you need to do
to get the best outcome.

125
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:01,560
Okay.

126
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:14,440
Hey.

127
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:17,640
Hey.

128
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:20,039
Hey.

129
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:21,960
I need one more favor.

130
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:25,480
My scrapbook is in the car, right?

131
00:11:26,280 --> 00:11:27,160
You can't.

132
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,239
I haven't even said anything.

133
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:32,879
You don't have to. I know what you want.

134
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,360
You want to...

135
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:39,399
You want to visit your aunt,

136
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:41,080
so you're using the scrapbook
as an excuse.

137
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:46,640
I didn't even say I wanted to.

138
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:49,279
I know my duty.

139
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:50,640
I know what I have to do today.

140
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:53,240
I was gonna ask you to go in my place.

141
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:56,919
But today is your first day back.

142
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:58,879
I don't want to leave you by yourself.

143
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:00,999
I get that.

144
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,720
But my aunt can't wait.

145
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:07,880
Right now, every second counts for her.

146
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:13,000
Please take that scrapbook to her for me.

147
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:16,480
Maybe...

148
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:21,880
she'll remember something and feel better.

149
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,639
Come on, I'll show you that

150
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:48,680
I can pull off
your elegant and fabulous demeanor.

151
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:01,600
Mr. Chris?

152
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:04,640
- Did you need something?
- Oh, I figured

153
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:09,439
it was your first day back at work,
so I wanted to congratulate you.

154
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:11,119
I see.

155
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:14,039
I wouldn't call it
my first day back at work.

156
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:16,240
It's more like therapy.

157
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:18,719
Grandpa and Chan wanted me here,

158
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:21,359
hoping it might help get my memory back.

159
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:22,679
Right.

160
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:24,880
I totally forgot you have amnesia.

161
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:29,279
But just seeing you back
makes me really happy.

162
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:33,559
Uh, Mr. Chan gave me
some documents to look over.

163
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:36,800
If there's nothing else,
I need to get back to work.

164
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:42,640
Ms. Claire,
do you remember your own secret?

165
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:48,760
My secret?

166
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:51,759
Yes.

167
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:54,400
The secret that only you and I know.

168
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,120
What did you say?

169
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:06,359
Our PR team told you to take down
the video from your website?

170
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,720
<i>You're a fraud!</i>

171
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:09,440
Ms. Rose,

172
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:13,360
even if you take it down,
people can still share it.

173
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:16,839
Well, that's for you to decide.

174
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,479
That woman?

175
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:23,240
She's probably a friend of the woman
who died in the crash.

176
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:26,679
But how you want to spin the story
is entirely up to you.

177
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:28,479
I have only one request.

178
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:31,840
My company and I must not be involved.

179
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:44,440
Chris.

180
00:14:57,880 --> 00:15:00,440
CHA

181
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:04,920
Where is he?

182
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:07,720
Why did he leave the phone here?

183
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:17,520
Chris?

184
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:30,280
Get me the facilities department
I want to check the security footage.

185
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:43,280
Where are we going?

186
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:47,400
To a place that will bring
your memory back.

187
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:52,520
Please.

188
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,319
I have to apologize.

189
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:03,560
I took the liberty of
grabbing your access card.

190
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,440
After you.

191
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:27,920
This is a restricted floor,
accessible only to C-level executives.

192
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:31,279
What's on this floor?

193
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:33,160
It sounds so mysterious.

194
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:37,560
It's where the company keeps
its confidential documents.

195
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:39,480
Especially this room.

196
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,200
What room is it?

197
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:48,000
Do you really not remember this room?

198
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:52,600
It's where you keep all the company's
architectural drawings.

199
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:57,880
You mean like the ones
for housing and condo projects?

200
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:00,400
Are they that confidential?

201
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,240
What's so funny?

202
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:08,439
The first time you brought me up here,

203
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:10,520
I asked you the same question.

204
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,919
And you told me

205
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:15,999
these documents have to be kept
under extra-tight security

206
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:20,560
because if they leaked, our competitors
might copy them and beat us to market.

207
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:27,359
Are you starting to remember anything?

208
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:32,959
No.

209
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:34,519
It's gonna take some time.

210
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:36,600
Thank you for bringing me up here.

211
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,159
Let's head back down.

212
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:39,160
I need to get back to work.

213
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:40,960
Hold on, Ms. Claire.

214
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:47,360
Do you really not remember
what we were doing up here?

215
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:04,680
TWO YEARS AGO

216
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:07,040
Why did you bring me up here?

217
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:12,680
Why do you think I brought you
to a place where we'd be alone?

218
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:27,160
Someone's here.

219
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:30,840
I felt like playing
hide-and-seek with Cha.

220
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:34,599
<i>I wanted to see
if your girlfriend could find us.</i>

221
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,600
<i>I should leave.</i>

222
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:39,359
Hold on, what's the rush?

223
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:41,040
Isn't this kind of thrilling?

224
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:42,759
Ms. Claire,

225
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:46,520
you know what will happen
if Cha catches us here alone.

226
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:53,800
Claire!

227
00:18:57,840 --> 00:18:59,120
What will happen?

228
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:02,520
‎You!

229
00:19:13,080 --> 00:19:14,000
Claire!

230
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:15,720
Stop!

231
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:21,880
Stop!

232
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,520
Stop!

233
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:28,719
Claire! Open this door right now!

234
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:30,080
Open!

235
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:36,759
Claire!

236
00:19:36,760 --> 00:19:38,759
Will she be able to get in here?

237
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:40,199
Don't worry.

238
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:42,000
It's only accessible to me.

239
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:43,880
Claire!

240
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:45,840
Open!

241
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:48,800
See?

242
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:53,880
Isn't this exciting?

243
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:12,200
Claire!

244
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:23,480
Open!

245
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:29,480
Open!

246
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,040
Chris!

247
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:38,880
Did I really do that?

248
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:40,840
Yes.

249
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:43,879
That's the secret about you.

250
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,840
What are you doing?

251
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:48,160
Bringing your memory back.

252
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:51,040
Hey, stop it.

253
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:56,360
Stop doing this to me.

254
00:20:58,040 --> 00:21:00,600
I used to like you
because I thought you were a good guy.

255
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:06,359
Stay away from me.

256
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:08,880
I promised Cha I'd stay away from you.

257
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:10,439
Claire, come on.

258
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:12,959
But I miss you, Claire.

259
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:14,479
- Stop.
- Claire.

260
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:16,159
Hey, get off me!

261
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:17,359
No!

262
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:19,720
Get off me! Stop! Hey!

263
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:33,279
Cha.

264
00:21:33,280 --> 00:21:35,239
She has access to this floor too.

265
00:21:35,240 --> 00:21:36,800
Open the door now.

266
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,200
- What am I supposed to do?
- Look at the camera.

267
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:16,200
What are you doing?

268
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:18,000
Cha.

269
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:26,919
Uh, well...

270
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:28,799
I needed the Agriv drawings.

271
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:31,560
You know only Claire can unlock this room.

272
00:22:34,760 --> 00:22:35,919
Yes.

273
00:22:35,920 --> 00:22:39,080
We're here to see
the architectural drawings.

274
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:44,080
- Let's go.
- Hold on.

275
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:48,879
Open it then.

276
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:50,400
I'd love to see them too.

277
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:57,520
Sure.

278
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:38,199
I might not have looked
directly at the camera.

279
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,600
Let me try again.

280
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:41,440
Hey,

281
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:45,560
you know this security system
is top-of-the-line.

282
00:23:46,080 --> 00:23:49,080
It will lock us out
after three failed attempts.

283
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:54,160
We'll have to bring in technicians
from overseas to reset it.

284
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:01,240
I've already contacted them.

285
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:09,639
You might not have been informed,

286
00:24:09,640 --> 00:24:12,120
but the system
started acting up six months ago.

287
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:15,399
Since Ms. Claire was
recovering at the time,

288
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:17,240
I didn't bring them in.

289
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:19,599
Now that she's doing better,

290
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:22,920
they've confirmed
they'll be here within this month.

291
00:24:28,040 --> 00:24:29,880
Are you sure it's a system issue?

292
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,399
What do you mean by that?

293
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:35,760
You saw it yourself. It's a system issue.

294
00:24:39,320 --> 00:24:40,360
Besides,

295
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:43,480
what you're doing is inappropriate.

296
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:46,720
You shouldn't be giving Claire orders.

297
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:52,200
The only person who can
give her orders is the chairman.

298
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:03,080
If there's nothing else,

299
00:25:03,920 --> 00:25:05,640
it's best you head back downstairs.

300
00:25:35,080 --> 00:25:36,520
Why did you come up here?

301
00:25:37,320 --> 00:25:38,719
I didn't want to.

302
00:25:38,720 --> 00:25:40,839
Mr. Chris brought me here.

303
00:25:40,840 --> 00:25:44,439
He said Ms. Claire brought him up here,
so he showed me.

304
00:25:44,440 --> 00:25:46,680
He thought it'd bring back my memory.

305
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:51,760
Wait,

306
00:25:52,560 --> 00:25:56,960
you knew Ms. Claire and Mr. Chris
came up here together, didn't you?

307
00:26:01,600 --> 00:26:02,560
Let's head down.

308
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:04,600
Wait.

309
00:26:06,440 --> 00:26:08,480
How did you know I was up here?

310
00:26:12,360 --> 00:26:13,520
Claire!

311
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:21,440
KHAEDARUN KANTHARA
VICE PRESIDENT

312
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:25,600
Hey.

313
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:28,280
Thank you very much.

314
00:26:30,480 --> 00:26:35,120
Instead of thanking me,
you'd better start listening to me.

315
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:39,280
Can't you be nice for once?

316
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:42,959
Honestly, I didn't need to thank you.

317
00:26:42,960 --> 00:26:45,320
Because that scanner was already broken.

318
00:26:50,280 --> 00:26:52,120
The scanner isn't broken.

319
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:54,720
It's not?

320
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:58,359
Then why did my attempts fail?

321
00:26:58,360 --> 00:27:00,320
I have Ms. Claire's face.

322
00:27:03,280 --> 00:27:08,640
Because the system...
looks for Claire's iris, not yours.

323
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:13,920
Then what are you going to do?

324
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:17,560
We'll talk downstairs.

325
00:27:26,840 --> 00:27:29,559
I know we had our differences.

326
00:27:29,560 --> 00:27:31,680
But let's start over.

327
00:27:32,640 --> 00:27:33,680
Hello, everyone.

328
00:27:51,880 --> 00:27:55,600
Get me the engineer in charge of
the vault's security system.

329
00:28:00,560 --> 00:28:05,040
Chris, do you think the Claire we see
walking around is the real deal?

330
00:28:07,840 --> 00:28:09,440
Why do you ask that?

331
00:28:09,960 --> 00:28:15,439
I brought the technicians who installed
the vault's scanner in to check it.

332
00:28:15,440 --> 00:28:17,200
They said it worked fine.

333
00:28:19,080 --> 00:28:20,320
What does that mean?

334
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:26,439
Chris, have you ever wondered

335
00:28:26,440 --> 00:28:30,800
if the Claire we see walking around
is the real deal or an imposter?

336
00:28:33,080 --> 00:28:34,720
I still don't get it.

337
00:28:35,240 --> 00:28:36,879
We can see that it's her.

338
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:38,439
Sure.

339
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:42,319
She might look like her on the outside,
but who knows what's on the inside?

340
00:28:42,320 --> 00:28:43,679
And isn't it weird?

341
00:28:43,680 --> 00:28:45,639
Ever since Chan brought her back,

342
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:47,960
Claire's been acting weird.

343
00:28:49,040 --> 00:28:51,200
I mean, yeah, she's been weird,

344
00:28:52,320 --> 00:28:54,080
but she has amnesia.

345
00:28:56,280 --> 00:28:59,519
What if Chan got someone
to impersonate Claire

346
00:28:59,520 --> 00:29:01,320
and claim she has amnesia?

347
00:29:06,280 --> 00:29:10,800
Then how do we find out
if this Claire is real or fake?

348
00:29:14,680 --> 00:29:16,919
- Claire!
- Cha!

349
00:29:16,920 --> 00:29:19,160
- No!
- Cha, no! Cha!

350
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:26,359
How dare the two of you do this to me?

351
00:29:26,360 --> 00:29:28,599
Cha. Cha, please stop.

352
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:30,400
- Claire! You!
- Cha!

353
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:33,000
- Stop it, Cha.
- How does it feel?

354
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:38,919
Being done this dirty
by the guy you're head over heels for?

355
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:40,200
Does it hurt?

356
00:29:43,440 --> 00:29:45,279
- I'm gonna kill you!
- Cha!

357
00:29:45,280 --> 00:29:46,959
- Stop, Cha.
- No!

358
00:29:46,960 --> 00:29:48,039
- Cha.
- Let go!

359
00:29:48,040 --> 00:29:52,320
- Cha.
- Get off me!

360
00:29:52,920 --> 00:29:55,199
Why are you so mad?

361
00:29:55,200 --> 00:29:57,760
You should be thanking me instead.

362
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:05,360
- Stop, Cha.
- Let go!

363
00:30:07,080 --> 00:30:08,599
- Cha! Cha!
- Claire!

364
00:30:08,600 --> 00:30:10,640
Cha! Cha, no! Cha!

365
00:30:39,320 --> 00:30:44,160
If she's the real Claire,
she'll have a scar on her back.

366
00:31:01,440 --> 00:31:02,880
Hold on. Hey.

367
00:31:04,080 --> 00:31:06,720
Do you think Ms. Cha told
the chairman about the vault?

368
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:10,880
No.

369
00:31:11,640 --> 00:31:14,480
She knows how much he loves Claire.

370
00:31:15,080 --> 00:31:17,479
She wouldn't do anything without proof.

371
00:31:17,480 --> 00:31:19,040
It's too risky.

372
00:31:21,200 --> 00:31:25,479
But I still don't get why Ms. Claire
wanted to beat Ms. Cha so badly

373
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:27,200
that she would sleep with...

374
00:31:32,840 --> 00:31:33,720
Whatever.

375
00:31:34,520 --> 00:31:37,759
If that was the case,
why didn't she just ask her grandfather

376
00:31:37,760 --> 00:31:39,959
to kick Ms. Cha
and Aunt Rin out of the house?

377
00:31:39,960 --> 00:31:42,240
Why tolerate living under the same roof?

378
00:31:49,640 --> 00:31:51,080
It's because of the will.

379
00:31:52,720 --> 00:31:53,920
The will?

380
00:31:55,440 --> 00:31:57,960
<i>You two told him
to change the will, didn't you?</i>

381
00:32:02,240 --> 00:32:04,919
Claire, listen to me.

382
00:32:04,920 --> 00:32:10,440
Cha and I had no idea
why Mr. Thiwa called Mr. Suthee over.

383
00:32:11,280 --> 00:32:16,560
But we never told Mr. Thiwa
to change the will like you think.

384
00:32:17,160 --> 00:32:18,399
Really?

385
00:32:18,400 --> 00:32:19,679
If that's true,

386
00:32:19,680 --> 00:32:23,000
are you two standing here
to beg him for a handout?

387
00:32:24,720 --> 00:32:26,200
A handout?

388
00:32:28,360 --> 00:32:29,479
Mom,

389
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:34,039
maybe Dad really did call
the lawyer to change the will.

390
00:32:34,040 --> 00:32:36,559
Because he loves you very much,

391
00:32:36,560 --> 00:32:41,040
and he can't stand seeing anyone hurt her.

392
00:32:41,920 --> 00:32:46,040
When that time comes, who knows
who'll be begging who for a handout.

393
00:32:47,560 --> 00:32:48,880
No way.

394
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:51,440
He'd never choose you two over me.

395
00:32:52,440 --> 00:32:54,399
If you really believe that,

396
00:32:54,400 --> 00:32:56,760
why are you acting like a scalded dog?

397
00:32:58,760 --> 00:33:00,359
But don't you worry.

398
00:33:00,360 --> 00:33:03,440
If Dad really leaves everything
to the two of us,

399
00:33:03,960 --> 00:33:05,959
when the time comes,

400
00:33:05,960 --> 00:33:10,040
I'll donate some money to
the mental asylum you'll be staying in.

401
00:33:11,080 --> 00:33:11,920
You bitch.

402
00:33:12,440 --> 00:33:14,639
- What?
- Claire! Claire!

403
00:33:14,640 --> 00:33:15,559
- Wanna try me?
- Claire.

404
00:33:15,560 --> 00:33:17,519
- Why not?
- Please stop. Stop, stop.

405
00:33:17,520 --> 00:33:19,079
- Stop.
- Chan, Chan, let go. I said...

406
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:20,600
- Let go of me.
- What is all this racket?!

407
00:33:21,120 --> 00:33:23,040
Didn't you know we were talking?

408
00:33:29,920 --> 00:33:31,479
Please take care of it, Mr. Suthee.

409
00:33:31,480 --> 00:33:34,200
Yes, sir. I'll take my leave.

410
00:33:38,120 --> 00:33:40,080
Why did you call Mr. Suthee over?

411
00:33:41,840 --> 00:33:43,680
I just wanted to tweak the will.

412
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:45,840
Tweak the will?

413
00:33:46,560 --> 00:33:47,840
Why?

414
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:50,200
Did someone make you?

415
00:33:54,080 --> 00:33:58,160
You're not legally married to him,
so you made him change the will.

416
00:33:58,760 --> 00:34:00,480
I told you my mom didn't do it.

417
00:34:01,080 --> 00:34:02,599
Cut the crap.

418
00:34:02,600 --> 00:34:06,279
Anyone can see you two are dying
to get your hands on his fortune.

419
00:34:06,280 --> 00:34:07,560
Claire!

420
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:12,800
Nobody can make me do anything.

421
00:34:13,400 --> 00:34:16,360
If I were to leave
a part of my estate to Cha,

422
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:18,359
it wouldn't be all that strange.

423
00:34:18,360 --> 00:34:20,600
Since Aunt Rin is my wife,

424
00:34:21,320 --> 00:34:22,800
Cha's like my own child.

425
00:34:23,639 --> 00:34:25,920
Are you saying...

426
00:34:27,520 --> 00:34:29,360
you're gonna leave them the inheritance?

427
00:34:29,960 --> 00:34:33,480
Everything will only be revealed
after I'm dead.

428
00:34:35,480 --> 00:34:37,159
What does that mean, honey?

429
00:34:44,760 --> 00:34:45,919
I get it now.

430
00:34:45,920 --> 00:34:49,519
Everyone thinks he's going to leave
the inheritance to the other side.

431
00:34:49,520 --> 00:34:51,999
So they tolerate living together.

432
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:54,319
And both sides
have to do whatever it takes

433
00:34:54,320 --> 00:34:57,119
to make the other side
miserable enough to leave.

434
00:34:57,120 --> 00:34:58,360
Hey.

435
00:34:59,520 --> 00:35:03,200
Then Ms. Cha will never
let the vault thing slide.

436
00:35:04,760 --> 00:35:06,240
Have you thought of a plan?

437
00:35:13,760 --> 00:35:14,600
What?

438
00:35:17,520 --> 00:35:18,359
Hey.

439
00:35:18,360 --> 00:35:21,560
What? Hey. Hey.

440
00:35:24,880 --> 00:35:26,440
Hey, wait.

441
00:35:27,240 --> 00:35:28,799
You didn't answer me.

442
00:35:28,800 --> 00:35:30,360
How was it, Claire?

443
00:35:31,440 --> 00:35:32,760
Your first day on the job.

444
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:35,999
Uh, it went okay.

445
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:37,920
Get any memory back?

446
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:41,319
Not much, sir.

447
00:35:41,320 --> 00:35:43,200
She only recalled one thing,

448
00:35:43,880 --> 00:35:45,640
how to boss me around.

449
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:53,160
You're still up, Grandpa.

450
00:35:54,440 --> 00:35:58,080
I was staying up
to ask how your first day went.

451
00:35:59,040 --> 00:36:02,040
And I wanted to discuss
some business with Chan.

452
00:36:05,280 --> 00:36:07,000
Let me talk to him for a bit.

453
00:36:09,120 --> 00:36:10,080
Go get some rest.

454
00:36:10,680 --> 00:36:11,680
Come on, Chan.

455
00:36:12,200 --> 00:36:13,120
Yes, sir.

456
00:36:17,920 --> 00:36:19,600
What do you think he wants to talk about?

457
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:23,520
It's nothing.

458
00:36:24,040 --> 00:36:27,519
It's my job to give him daily updates
on company business.

459
00:36:27,520 --> 00:36:29,960
You had a long day. Go get some rest.

460
00:36:48,200 --> 00:36:50,080
Can you guess what I wanted to talk about?

461
00:36:52,160 --> 00:36:55,800
Is it about Claire hiring
those celebrities to be her friends?

462
00:36:56,400 --> 00:36:58,879
Her hiring those celebs to be her friends?

463
00:36:58,880 --> 00:37:00,239
That's so Claire!

464
00:37:00,240 --> 00:37:02,559
That didn't surprise me at all.

465
00:37:02,560 --> 00:37:05,160
What I actually wanted to talk to you

466
00:37:05,720 --> 00:37:08,560
is about the woman who ambushed Claire.

467
00:37:09,280 --> 00:37:12,719
How could her security be that lax?

468
00:37:12,720 --> 00:37:15,800
What if that woman had a gun?

469
00:37:17,520 --> 00:37:18,959
I apologize, sir.

470
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:22,239
But I've instructed the security
and facilities departments

471
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:24,439
to strictly screen everyone coming in.

472
00:37:24,440 --> 00:37:26,400
Of course you have.

473
00:37:27,560 --> 00:37:29,480
And how are you gonna handle that woman?

474
00:37:31,880 --> 00:37:33,440
I already handled it.

475
00:37:37,320 --> 00:37:40,160
Go wait outside. I'll talk to him.

476
00:37:41,960 --> 00:37:43,879
Please don't hurt Ms. Wan.

477
00:37:43,880 --> 00:37:45,520
She was just angry about her friend.

478
00:37:48,360 --> 00:37:49,959
Who said I would hurt her?

479
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:52,080
I have no intention of hurting her.

480
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:55,560
Oh, then...

481
00:37:56,200 --> 00:38:01,840
what did you mean when you asked him
how we were going to handle her?

482
00:38:03,720 --> 00:38:06,000
I was referring to the woman named Jinla.

483
00:38:12,520 --> 00:38:15,680
When I saw the news today,
I had my people look into her.

484
00:38:16,320 --> 00:38:20,559
But I just recalled that
the woman named Jinla

485
00:38:20,560 --> 00:38:22,400
was with you in the crash.

486
00:38:26,880 --> 00:38:30,400
Chan, do you know this woman Jinla?

487
00:38:34,560 --> 00:38:37,119
I don't know her personally, sir.

488
00:38:37,120 --> 00:38:41,360
I only know she was the one interviewing
Claire on the day of the crash.

489
00:38:42,400 --> 00:38:44,480
Is there something on your mind?

490
00:38:50,880 --> 00:38:52,320
Poor woman.

491
00:38:55,240 --> 00:38:57,160
She lived with her aunt.

492
00:38:58,560 --> 00:39:00,160
And when she passed away,

493
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:03,560
her aunt ended up...

494
00:39:10,280 --> 00:39:11,880
Grandpa, are you okay?

495
00:39:16,760 --> 00:39:17,920
I'm fine.

496
00:39:21,920 --> 00:39:25,040
Her aunt must've loved her
just as much as I love you.

497
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:30,560
And if I were her aunt,
I wouldn't be able to cope either.

498
00:39:32,960 --> 00:39:34,920
If her aunt were still around,

499
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:38,520
I'd have offered her
some financial relief.

500
00:39:41,080 --> 00:39:42,240
Hey, Chan.

501
00:39:43,280 --> 00:39:47,080
I want you to look after her affairs,
even though she's gone.

502
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:51,320
Help those around her as best as we can.

503
00:39:53,520 --> 00:39:54,440
Understood.

504
00:39:57,000 --> 00:39:58,360
As for you,

505
00:39:59,680 --> 00:40:03,080
live your life from now on,
knowing its true value.

506
00:40:04,560 --> 00:40:09,080
Because many people don't get
a second chance at life like you did.

507
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:12,880
I will.

508
00:40:14,480 --> 00:40:15,519
Go get some rest.

509
00:40:15,520 --> 00:40:17,280
That's all I wanted to talk about.

510
00:40:25,520 --> 00:40:26,600
Oh, Chan.

511
00:40:28,440 --> 00:40:29,280
Sir?

512
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:33,640
I hope you haven't forgotten
the promise you made to me.

513
00:40:38,160 --> 00:40:39,200
I have not.

514
00:40:54,640 --> 00:40:56,400
Aren't you gonna walk me to my room?

515
00:40:59,400 --> 00:41:00,919
You're doing great now.

516
00:41:00,920 --> 00:41:03,360
Walking there alone should be a breeze.

517
00:41:04,320 --> 00:41:06,120
What are you mad at me for?

518
00:41:06,960 --> 00:41:08,240
I see.

519
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:12,760
You're mad because
I eavesdropped on your conversation.

520
00:41:14,920 --> 00:41:20,039
And the way you popped out like that
and acted all chummy with Ms. Wan,

521
00:41:20,040 --> 00:41:22,160
you don't think he'd find that suspicious?

522
00:41:24,880 --> 00:41:29,560
Well, I was afraid he would order you
to do something to Wan.

523
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:33,599
Order me to do something to her?

524
00:41:33,600 --> 00:41:37,239
You seriously think
he would order me to hurt her or kill her?

525
00:41:37,240 --> 00:41:40,399
Hey, this is real life, not a drama.

526
00:41:40,400 --> 00:41:43,039
How could we just kill someone, huh?

527
00:41:43,040 --> 00:41:44,679
Really?

528
00:41:44,680 --> 00:41:46,319
What about what you did to me?

529
00:41:46,320 --> 00:41:49,400
It was basically the same as killing me.

530
00:41:50,040 --> 00:41:51,599
You talk back a lot these days.

531
00:41:51,600 --> 00:41:53,359
If you don't want me to,

532
00:41:53,360 --> 00:41:56,640
you should've sewn my mouth shut
when you changed my face.

533
00:41:58,640 --> 00:42:01,640
With your smart mouth,
walk to your room yourself.

534
00:42:05,520 --> 00:42:07,520
Do you think I can't manage?

535
00:42:09,200 --> 00:42:11,600
It's just right there. Whatever.

536
00:42:40,040 --> 00:42:43,360
<i>I hope you haven't forgotten
the promise you made to me.</i>

537
00:42:48,160 --> 00:42:54,080
I, NITCHAN SATHITPHONG, PROMISE THAT
I WILL ONLY MARRY KHAEDARUN KANCHATHARA.

538
00:42:54,680 --> 00:42:55,880
Give me your hand.

539
00:43:04,480 --> 00:43:08,360
I, NITCHAN SATHITPHONG, PROMISE THAT
I WILL ONLY MARRY KHAEDARUN KANCHATHARA.

540
00:43:25,720 --> 00:43:27,840
I came to tell you to do your job.

541
00:43:29,640 --> 00:43:31,319
You haven't checked my room yet.

542
00:43:31,320 --> 00:43:34,040
Aren't you going to check
if anyone snuck in there?

543
